  "limits": "One real UK Biobank subject, also used to screen the optimizer settings; no independent subject validation. FNIT runs registration on GPU and official MSM on CPU, so speed figures are not matched hardware comparisons. FNIT uses a continuous sulc-MSE optimizer with 2562 Fibonacci controls and an approximate triangle-strain penalty; it does not reproduce the official multilevel discrete HOCR objective, and its default sphere is not numerically equivalent. Upstream BBR, MNI registration and denoising differ from fMRIPrep."
